hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18947","Waki and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, Ibn Jafar said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari narrating, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade plunder and mutilation."
"18948","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every good deed is charity."
"18949","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shubah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, and he is al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade plunder and mutilation."
